# =============================================================================
# ROOT .dockerignore — this is the ONLY .dockerignore Docker honours, because
# both images build with the repository root as the build context
# (see backend/Dockerfile & frontend/Dockerfile). The per-package
# backend/.dockerignore and frontend/.dockerignore are NOT consulted for a
# root-context build, so all exclusions must live here.
#
# Primary purpose: keep real secrets (.env), the .git history, and heavy docs
# OUT of the build context so they can never be COPYed into an image layer.
# =============================================================================

# Secrets — never ship real env files into the build context.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example
!.env.docker.example

# VCS & tooling
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.claude
.idea

# Dependencies & build output (images run `npm ci` / build fresh)
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage

# Docs (not needed at runtime; ~500 KB of markdown)
*.md
backend/*.md
frontend/*.md

# Logs & OS cruft
**/npm-debug.log*
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local compose/runtime artifacts
docker-compose*.yml
